Write a function to find the longest common prefix string amongst an array of strings.
If there is no common prefix, return an empty string "".
Example 1
Input : str = ["flowers" , "flow" , "fly", "flight" ]
Output : "fl"
Explanation :
All strings given in array contains common prefix "fl".
Example 2
Input : str = ["dog" , "cat" , "animal", "monkey" ]
Output : ""
Explanation :
There is no common prefix among the given strings in array.

Constraints:
1 <= str.length <= 200
1 <= str[i].length <= 200
str[i] contains only lowercase English letters.



//code
class Solution {    
    public String longestCommonPrefix(String[] str) {
        //your code goes here
        String ans="";
        int stop=1,i=0;
        while(stop==1){
            int c=0;
            for(String s:str){
                if (i >= s.length()) {
                    stop = 0;
                    break;
                }
                if(s.charAt(i)!=str[0].charAt(i)){
                    c=1;
                    stop=0;
                    break;
                }
            }
            if(c==0 && stop==1) {
                ans = ans+str[0].charAt(i);
                i++;
            }
        }
        return ans;
    }
}
